#4471 holds **412 unique reports** (the export has 427 rows; 15 are repeats of the same id).
They are not one bug. The cause depends on the tenant, not on what intake tagged.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## 1. Parser reads month first: 379 reports

The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants (all 11 on file) get their
dates flipped. This is what #4471 was filed for. It includes the 5 reports the desk read as a
one-day move; by tenant they belong here. Ticket:
[capstone#1](https://github.com/Infinity0106/capstone/issues/1).

## 2. booking-v3 form hint: 33 reports

`copper.studio`, `alder.physio` and `pale.harbour` run booking-v3, which prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
under the date field. Their people type month first, as told, and the form reads it day first.
Fixing the parser does not fix this. It has no ticket of its own on the desk; it was merged
into #4471. Ticket: [capstone#2](https://github.com/Infinity0106/capstone/issues/2).

<Callout>
Intake's tag is a guess from the browser. It is wrong for 23 parser reports (tagged hint) and
15 hint reports (tagged parser). Count by tenant and channel.
</Callout>

